# LIBRARY: own
# The then of its own is laid on the operand BEHIND the call that handed it back: at the call the cell is still as made. So the cell is asked at the use, not where the note is laid.
# The lie, testing=OneRowSpeaksForAllThatCallMayTake: where a call may take several rows the first alone is asked whether what it hands back is fresh, though another hands back the operand: the result is noted as made. Under testing=CheckProofsAtRunTime (--aot-harden=proof-checks) the cell is asked where the note is leaned on: the process stops by name.
# RUN(RIGHT): run-in-shell mechanisms=all
# RIGHT: own
# RIGHT-NEXT: exited with 0
# RUN(HARDENED): run-in-shell mechanisms=all testing=CheckProofsAtRunTime
# HARDENED: own
# HARDENED-NEXT: exited with 0
# RUN(LIE): run-in-shell mechanisms=all testing=CheckProofsAtRunTime,OneRowSpeaksForAllThatCallMayTake
# LIE: AOT: f{{*}} at {{*}}: what memory holds where the compiler remembers another value is not of the type that the compiler has proven of it. It is: another value or a test that once passed fails. This is a bug in Bun.
